        "text": "Flåmsdalen is a valley in Aurland Municipality in Vestland county, Norway. It is 18 kilometers (11 mi) long and runs from Myrdal to the village of Flåm, dropping 860 meters (2,820 ft) over the course of its run. The river Flåmselvi runs through the valley, as does the Flåm Line, a famous tourist destination.\n\n\n== Media gallery ==\n\n\n== References ==\n\n\n== External links ==\n Media related to Flåmsdalen at Wikimedia Commons",
